  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Oxaceprol is a chemical compound that has been described as a disease-modifying antirheumatic drug and a dermatologic drug, with ATC codes for non-steroidal antiinflammatory and antirheumatic agents and other dermatological preparations. It appears only as an experimental status in drug databases, with no EMA authorisation, so its current availability is unclear.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q408948&quot;>Wikidata Q408948</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>oxaceprol</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>D11AX09, M01AX24</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB13363&quot;>DB13363</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/65784&quot;>65784</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q408948&quot;>Q408948</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C7H11NO4</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>173.168 g/mol (PubChem)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
